  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find the sum\n$$\\sin^2 0^\\circ+\\sin^2 1^\\circ+\\sin^2 2^\\circ+\\cdots+\\sin^2 89^\\circ+\\sin^2 90^\\circ.$$\nHint: Use $\\sin(90-\\theta)^\\circ=\\cos(\\theta^\\circ)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$45.5$.\n\nThe 45 complementary pairs each sum to 1; the remaining term is $\\sin^2 45^\\circ=\\tfrac12$.",
      "worked": "Pair each term from $\\sin^2 0^\\circ$ to $\\sin^2 44^\\circ$ with its complementary-angle term:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^2\\theta^\\circ+\\sin^2(90-\\theta)^\\circ&=\\sin^2\\theta^\\circ+\\cos^2\\theta^\\circ\\\\\\sin^2\\theta^\\circ+\\sin^2(90-\\theta)^\\circ&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 45 such pairs. The unpaired middle term is $\\sin^2 45^\\circ=\\tfrac12$. Thus,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^2 0^\\circ+\\sin^2 1^\\circ+\\cdots+\\sin^2 90^\\circ&=45+\\frac12\\\\\\sin^2 0^\\circ+\\sin^2 1^\\circ+\\cdots+\\sin^2 90^\\circ&=45.5.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
